    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34385" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pējōro</span></b> , āre
		pejor, v. a. and n. (postclass.).
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to render worse</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">statum suum pejorare, opp. to meliorem facere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Paul. Sent. 2</span></i>
			, tit. 18.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to grow worse</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pejorans morbus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Acut. 2, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Tard. 2, 1 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
